1
00:00:00,829 --> 00:00:02,129
(Raj:)that NASA's been
working on?
Yeah.

2
00:00:02,130 --> 00:00:04,400
(Raj:)Well, they're looking
to include a message from Earth

3
00:00:04,399 --> 00:00:07,539
(Raj:)in case one of them
is encountered by alien life.
LEONARD: Oh.

4
00:00:07,536 --> 00:00:09,536
(Leonard:)When I encountered alien life,
I-I discovered

5
00:00:09,538 --> 00:00:13,078
(Leonard:)that the key thing
was not to sit in its spot.

6
00:00:13,075 --> 00:00:16,845
(Sheldon:)All right, you can't breathe
our air without an inhaler,

7
00:00:16,845 --> 00:00:18,575
(Sheldon:)he's allergic
to Earth nuts,

8
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:19,810
(Sheldon:)but I'm the alien.

9
00:00:19,815 --> 00:00:21,815
KOOTHRAPPALI:
Anyway,

10
00:00:21,817 --> 00:00:23,617
(Raj:)I'm among a handful
of scientists

11
00:00:23,618 --> 00:00:25,888
(Raj:)that have been asked to submit
a design proposal

12
00:00:25,887 --> 00:00:28,057
(Raj:)for the message
and its delivery system.

13
00:00:28,056 --> 00:00:30,026
(Sheldon:)Excellent.
Congratulations.
Good for you.

14
00:00:30,025 --> 00:00:32,095
(Raj:)And I was wondering
if any of you guys

15
00:00:32,094 --> 00:00:34,064
(Raj:)would like
to help me do it.

16
00:00:34,062 --> 00:00:36,262
(Leonard:)Are you kidding? Yes.
What did you have in mind?

17
00:00:36,264 --> 00:00:39,104
(Sheldon:)I'll tell you exactly what you
should do: avoid the presumption

18
00:00:39,101 --> 00:00:42,101
(Sheldon:)of the Terran sensory
input paradigm.
WOLOWITZ: Yeah, absolutely.

19
00:00:42,104 --> 00:00:43,974
(Howard:)You need a device capable
of delivering information

20
00:00:43,972 --> 00:00:46,672
(Howard:)across a wide range
of perceptual modalities.

21
00:00:46,675 --> 00:00:49,345
(Sheldon:)Any intelligent organism
would at the very least need

22
00:00:49,344 --> 00:00:51,674
(Sheldon:)the ability to locate the
position of objects in space.

23
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:55,520
(Sheldon:)So the ideal interstellar
lingua franca would be haptic.

24
00:00:55,517 --> 00:00:57,517
(Howard:)Ooh, how about a 3-D
tactile communicator rigged

25
00:00:57,519 --> 00:00:59,189
(Howard:)for cross-sensory transposition?

26
00:00:59,187 --> 00:01:00,457
(Raj:)Exactly what I expected.

27
00:01:00,455 --> 00:01:02,155
(Raj:)Two people
forcing their ideas on me

28
00:01:02,157 --> 00:01:03,957
(Raj:)and only one gentleman
who could be bothered

29
00:01:03,959 --> 00:01:05,489
(Raj:)to ask me what my thoughts were.

30
00:01:05,494 --> 00:01:07,494
(Raj:)You two are out.
Congratulations, Leonard,

31
00:01:07,496 --> 00:01:09,126
(Raj:)you're on the team.

32
00:01:09,930 --> 00:01:13,100
(Leonard:)My mommy raised a gentleman.

